WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
JENNY BROWN: Today we're talking
about code secrets, health care

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.370
consent, no-code hackathons,
and new podcasts.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.190
I'm Jenny Brown, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.610
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.190
Secret Manager is a
Google Cloud service

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.560
that provides a secure
and convenient method

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.920
for storing API keys,
passwords, certificates,

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.780
and other sensitive data.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.140
Secret Manager provides a
central place and single source

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.990
of truth to manage,
access, and audit secrets

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.640
across Google Cloud.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.740
The integration with
Cloud Code brings

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.250
those powerful capabilities
to your preferred IDE.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.650
Check out the post or
video to learn more

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:43.040
about how to make your
code as secure as possible.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.380
The Health Care
Consent Management API

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.740
is now generally available,
giving customers the ability

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.740
to greatly scale the
management of patient consent

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.410
to meet increasing
need, particularly

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.660
amidst the emerging
task of managing health

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.480
data for new care and
research scenarios.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.910
To learn more, check
out the full post.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.940
Hackathons are a great way to
mix things up and supercharge

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.560
your brainstorming,
and with no-code tools,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.980
non-technical
employees can transform

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.580
into citizen developers who
are empowered to use technology

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.440
to build creative solutions.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.800
AppSheet, Google Cloud's
no-code application development

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.590
platform, is a game changer,
so check out the blog

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.430
to learn more.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.700
Google Cloud Reader
is an audio companion

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.860
to many of the posts
on our tech blog.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.560
With new episodes on
Tuesdays and Thursdays,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.590
you'll be able to hear about
a range of topics from cloud

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.270
storage to machine learning.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.700
No matter why you
prefer an audio format,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.090
we've got you covered.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:43.640
Check it out wherever
you listen to podcasts.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.760
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.440
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.960
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.680
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.910
We'll see you in the Cloud.

